<===> README.md
Like dart-sass, a style rule without a selector errors with `expected end of
rule.` if nothing follows (e.g. an unclosed block), otherwise with
`unrecognized syntax`.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> error/unclosed/multiline/input.scss
a {
  b: c;
<===> error/unclosed/multiline/error
Error: expected end of rule.
  ,
2 |   b: c;
  |        ^
  '
  input.scss 2:8  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> error/unclosed/nested/input.scss
a {b {c: d}
<===> error/unclosed/nested/error
Error: expected end of rule.
  ,
1 | a {b {c: d}
  |            ^
  '
  input.scss 1:12  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> error/unrecognized/after_declaration/input.scss
a {b: c; !x}
<===> error/unrecognized/after_declaration/error
Error: unrecognized syntax
  ,
1 | a {b: c; !x}
  |          ^^
  '
  input.scss 1:10  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> error/unrecognized/first/input.scss
a { !x }
<===> error/unrecognized/first/error
Error: unrecognized syntax
  ,
1 | a { !x }
  |     ^^^
  '
  input.scss 1:5  root stylesheet
